<p>Writing is safe: whether the real list is of <code>Integer</code>, <code>Number</code> or <code>Object</code>, an <code>Integer</code> fits. One <code>themSo</code> fills all three lists — look at the output: the <code>List&lt;Number&gt;</code> already held <code>0.5</code>, the <code>List&lt;Object&gt;</code> already held <code>"x"</code>. That is also why reading is weak: the first element may be a <code>Double</code> or a <code>String</code>, so the only type javac can promise is <code>Object</code>, and <code>Integer first = xs.get(0)</code> fails with "CAP#1 cannot be converted to Integer" (this time <code>CAP#1</code> is "Object super: Integer").</p>
