<p>(1) <strong>Swallowed</strong>: the empty <code>catch</code> turns "file not found" into <code>null</code>, and the program fails much later with a <code>NullPointerException</code> whose message talks about <code>&lt;local1&gt;</code> — the real cause is gone. (2) <strong>Cause lost</strong>: <code>new IllegalStateException("…" + e.getMessage())</code> keeps the text but drops the exception, so <code>getCause()</code> is <code>null</code> and the stack trace of the original failure is lost; passing <code>e</code> as the second argument keeps it.</p>
