<p>Levels: JUL has SEVERE, WARNING, INFO, CONFIG, FINE, FINER, FINEST. With the logger at INFO, the two FINE lines print nothing; set it to FINE and the same code prints them; set it to WARNING and the INFO line disappears while SEVERE stays. That one setting is what <code>System.out.println</code> can never give you — the last output line prints no matter what.</p>
